# Every setting is optional. Copy to .env.local and uncomment what you need.

# Where the SQLite database lives (default: ./data/innkeep.db)
# DATABASE_PATH=/var/lib/innkeep/innkeep.db

# A hosted Turso database instead of the file, for a host with no disk of
# its own such as Vercel. See docs/DEPLOY.md.
# TURSO_DATABASE_URL=libsql://your-database.turso.io
# TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Only with Turso, and only if more than one account should be able to sign
# up: each account after the first gets a database of its own, which Innkeep
# creates through Turso's API. The organisation's slug, an API token, the
# group to create them in, and a token for that group. Without these, the
# first account works and a second sign-up is refused.
# TURSO_ORG=
# TURSO_API_TOKEN=
# TURSO_GROUP=default
# TURSO_GROUP_TOKEN=

# Lets a scheduler run the calendar sync and the notifications by calling
# GET /api/cron with "Authorization: Bearer <this value>". Only needed on a
# serverless host, where the built-in timer cannot run.
# CRON_SECRET=

# Public address of this instance, used to build calendar export links.
# Needed when the app sits behind a proxy that hides the original host.
# APP_URL=https://innkeep.example.com

# Minutes between background calendar syncs (default 15, 0 disables).
# SYNC_INTERVAL_MINUTES=15

# Turns on AI advice on the Suggestions page (https://console.anthropic.com).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# AI_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5

# Turns on the MCP server at /api/mcp for AI assistants.
# MCP_TOKEN=

# Turns on POST /api/ingest/reservations for the Innkeep browser extension.
# EXTENSION_TOKEN=

# Once the extension is on the Chrome Web Store (docs/CHROME-WEB-STORE.md): its
# address there. The setup guide then offers "Install" in place of "Load unpacked".
# EXTENSION_STORE_URL=

# Everyone signs in with an account of their own: nothing to set for that.
# SIGN_UP=closed stops new accounts once you have yours (invitations still
# work). SESSION_SECRET signs the sessions; left unset, Innkeep makes one and
# keeps it in its database.
# SIGN_UP=closed
# SESSION_SECRET=

# Only when upgrading an Innkeep that used this password before accounts
# existed: it no longer signs anyone in. Type it once in "Password of this
# Innkeep" when you create your account, to take your properties and bookings
# with you. Remove it afterwards.
# APP_PASSWORD=

# Sends a Telegram message each time a cleaning has to be arranged.
# Create a bot with @BotFather for the token; the chat is you or a group the
# bot belongs to. See docs/DEPLOY.md for the steps.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Optional: the chat's number. Without it, pick the chat on the Settings page.
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# TELEGRAM_LANGUAGE=fr

# Shows a public demo next to your own Innkeep. A visitor who is not signed
# in gets the public pages and a read-only dashboard on sample bookings, kept
# in memory and apart from everyone's data. The landing page then takes
# early-access requests, as with LANDING_ONLY. Leave unset to send everyone
# who is not signed in to the sign-in page.
# PUBLIC_DEMO=1

# Publishes only the landing, Alternatives and guide pages: the dashboard and
# every API route answer "not found". For a public website; leave unset to run
# Innkeep. The landing page then takes early-access requests and sends each one
# to TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID through TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN (both are needed there).
# LANDING_ONLY=1
